edb/ref 17592186436949 13194139534814 17592186045417 true] [17592186436950 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534814 17592186045417 true] [17592186436950 1077 "selection" 13194139534814 17592186045417 true] [17592186436950 1078 #edb/ref 17592186436943 13194139534814 17592186045417 true] [17592186436950 1079 #uuid "aee200cc-d9b2-5d5b-a23a-38088da4f688" 13194139534814 17592186045417 true] [17592186436951 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436950 13194139534814 17592186045417 true] [17592186436951 1069 "q-64967" 13194139534814 17592186045417 true] [17592186436951 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534814 17592186045417 true] [17592186436951 1071 "A surface $S$ is defined by $z=f(x,y).$ The curve $C$ is the intersection of $S$ with the plane $y=1.$ Given that the point $P$ with $x$-coordinate $\\pi $ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{x}=y{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)$, find the slope of the tangent to $C$ at $P.$" 13194139534814 17592186045417 true] [17592186436951 1072 #uuid "0063a739-db3e-5983-b65e-bb4c57fabf9c" 13194139534814 17592186045417 true] [17592186436951 1074 "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $y=1.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve $C$ at the point where $x=\\pi $ will be given by the partial derivative ${f}_{x}(\\pi ,1).$ \n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative ${f}_{x}(x,y)$ at $(\\pi ,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(\\pi ,1) & =(1){e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi \\cdot 1)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi \\cdot 1) \\\\  & ={e}^{0}(-1) \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534814 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-2df6297f-0710-55c1-aeca-d0bbd6193592" 17592186436940 "answer-3e1e7001-fa28-52e7-9159-e1a9952ad01c" 17592186436941 "answer-46868586-3cca-540f-a185-1309d5aab5a9" 17592186436942 "answer-5212a9fa-3e07-5070-b235-7a3b34cb5bd2" 17592186436943 "answer-7ba5571e-63b9-59ee-98ea-36a27b8aac00" 17592186436944 "answer-83e7b9f8-74d8-5b05-8940-fc35083f8350" 17592186436945 "answe